1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,700
This clip was drawn by a script, so it is free to share.

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,800
It shows what analysis-video pulls out of a lecture.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,600
A recording is thousands of frames that are nearly all the same.

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,800
And a transcript that never says what was on screen.

5
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,800
So the tool works in four moves, and I will write them out.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,600
Watch the board. Nothing here is a cut, the picture only grows.

7
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,400
Every frame is almost identical to the one before it.

8
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,400
A detector that only hunts for cuts would keep this empty board.

9
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,600
So a second signal measures the drift away from where it started.

10
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,400
And when the screen finally leaves, it is shot again, finished.

11
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:31,600
Each screen becomes one section of a Markdown file.

12
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,600
The seconds it was up, its images, and the words spoken over it.

13
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,600
You can rebuild this clip and rerun the whole pipeline yourself.

14
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,600
One command, no network, nothing but the file on your disk.
